  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef is now performing a thorough cleaning of every room in his house.\n\nChef's house has XXX small rooms and YYY large rooms.\n\nEach small room requires 303030 minutes to clean, and each large room requires 606060 minutes.\n\nHow many minutes does Chef need to clean his entire house?\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe only line of input contains two space-separated integers XXX and YYY — the number of small and large rooms in Chef's house, respectively.\n\n\nOutput Format\nOutput a single integer: the number of minutes Chef requires to clean his house.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤X,Y≤101 \\le X, Y \\le 101≤X,Y≤10"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4 3",
        "output": "300",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThere are 444 small rooms, each needing 303030 minutes to clean. The total time needed for the small rooms is hence 4×30=1204\\times 30 = 1204×30=120 minutes.\nThere are 333 large rooms, each needing 606060 minutes to clean. The total time needed for the large rooms is hence 3×60=1803\\times 60 = 1803×60=180 minutes.\nThe total time needed for all rooms is 120+180=300120 + 180 = 300120+180=300 minutes."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2 10",
        "output": "660",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThere are 222 small rooms, each needing 303030 minutes to clean. The total time needed for the small rooms is hence 2×30=602\\times 30 = 602×30=60 minutes.\nThere are 101010 large rooms, each needing 606060 minutes to clean. The total time needed for the large rooms is hence 10×60=60010\\times 60 = 60010×60=600 minutes.\nThe total time needed for all rooms is 60+600=66060 + 600 = 66060+600=660 minutes."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "7 3",
        "output": "390",
        "explanation": ""
      }
    ]
  },
